.\"
.\" QUICK_EXIT(3) - Substrate C Library
.\"
.TH QUICK_EXIT 3 "May 2026" "Substrate OS" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
quick_exit, at_quick_exit \- fast process termination
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, \-lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdlib.h>
.PP
.BI "int at_quick_exit(void (*" func ")(void));"
.BI "void quick_exit(int " status ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR quick_exit ()
function causes normal process termination without the cleanup that
.BR exit (3)
performs.
It calls every function registered with
.BR at_quick_exit ()
\(em in the reverse order of their registration \(em and then calls
.BR _Exit (3)
with the value of
.IR status .
.PP
Unlike
.BR exit (3),
.BR quick_exit ()
does
.B not
call functions registered with
.BR atexit (3),
does
.B not
run C++ or dynamic-linker destructors, and does
.B not
flush or close open
.B stdio
streams.
It is the minimal, predictable termination path for use when the
state of the program is such that the normal cleanup handlers cannot
safely run.
.PP
The
.BR at_quick_exit ()
function registers
.I func
to be called, without arguments, by
.BR quick_exit ().
The registration list maintained by
.BR at_quick_exit ()
is separate from the one used by
.BR atexit (3):
.BR quick_exit ()
runs only the functions registered here.
At least 32 functions can be registered.
.PP
If a registered function is itself registered more than once it is
called once for each registration.
A function registered by a handler that runs during
.BR quick_exit ()
processing is also called, after the handlers that had already run
when it was registered.
If a registered function does not return, the remaining registered
functions are not called.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR quick_exit ()
function does not return to its caller.
.PP
The
.BR at_quick_exit ()
function returns 0 if the registration succeeds, and a non-zero
value if it fails \(em because
.I func
is a null pointer, or because the registration list is already
full.
Neither function sets
.IR errno .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <unistd.h>

static void flush_log(void) { /* ... */ }

int main(void)
{
    if (at_quick_exit(flush_log) != 0)
        write(2, "registration failed\\n", 20);
    /* ... */
    quick_exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR _Exit (3),
.BR atexit (3),
.BR exit (3),
.BR abort (3)
.SH STANDARDS
.BR quick_exit ()
and
.BR at_quick_exit ()
conform to C11 (ISO/IEC 9899:2011, \(sc7.22.4) and C17.
